<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P) & Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics — Model fidelity to source: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements 3D nodal level-set potentials and analytical/finite-difference implicit-surface mean curvature H and Gaussian curvature K (`evaluate_tpms_field_and_curvature_3d`, L215-399) across Diamond D (Z=4, 109.4712 deg), Gyroid G (Z=3, 120 deg), Primitive P (Z=6, 90 deg), Cahn–Hilliard spinodal labyrinthic foam, and pinch-off ablation (c=1.35), plus crystallographic [111] vs [100] projections and edge dislocations (`evaluate_crystallographic_projections_and_dislocations`, L458-514) and Gibson–Ashby stretching vs bending mechanics (L520-599). Backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_079_crinoid_stereom_gyroid.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-model-fidelity-1>,
