<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Yang et al. (2022) & Donnay & Pawson (1969) biogenic single-crystal calcite TPMS echinoderm stereom (Diamond D, Gyroid G, Primitive P) & Gibson-Ashby cellular mechanics — MorphoEval overall 91.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) remediated evaluation of `2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py` (consensus score 91.8/100, up from 52.4/100 in Pass 1). The remediated script implements 3D nodal TPMS level-set geometry and exact implicit-surface mean and Gaussian curvature computation (`evaluate_tpms_field_and_curvature_3d`, L215-399) across Schwarz Diamond D (Z=4 tetrahedral nodes at 109.4712 deg), Schoen Gyroid G (Z=3 chiral trigonal nodes at 120 deg), Schwarz Primitive P (Z=6 orthogonal cubic nodes at 90 deg), Cahn–Hilliard spinodal labyrinthic stereom control, and super-threshold pinch-off ablation (c=1.35 -> Z=0), verifies zero mean curvature (|<H>|=5.16e-19), 100% hyperbolic saddle curvature (K<=0), exact 50% solid fraction at c=0 (phi(0)=0.5000), and genus-3 Euler characteristic chi=-4, models [111] vs [100] crystallographic projections and edge dislocations, validates Gibson–Ashby stretching (phi^1) vs bending (phi^2) stiffness across 12 Echinodermata species (r=0.9997), and segments the crinoid ossicle stereom SEM plate (phi_obs=0.5187, trabecular period a_0=14.80 um), backed by 4 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. Overall 91.7/100 (faithfulness 91.4, reproducibility 92.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit HEAD; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 90, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_comparison.png: rendered output of 2020-gorzelak-crinoid-stereom-gyroid.py at HEAD, image/png, 776113 B, 2084×1469 px, artifact_sha256 fa3a3bc5ea25717ac454178df9ad65455f74bccd7674102eb3fea9f9b83ffe0e (sha256 fa3a3bc5ea25717ac454178df9ad65455f74bccd7674102eb3fea9f9b83ffe0e), spec_fingerprint 7546780a29581d038c82edc49698f8e73b11c59c0a49d82e3dfc8f721733c9d2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7546780a29581d038c82edc49698f8e73b11c59c0a49d82e3dfc8f721733c9d2; artifact_sha256: fa3a3bc5ea25717ac454178df9ad65455f74bccd7674102eb3fea9f9b83ffe0e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_gyroid_reference.json=c1c3848ef15d0bfc..., datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/crinoid_stereom_ossicle_specimen.jpg=5fbf6e4db0ee1d44..., datasets/crinoid_stereom_gyroid/scout_manifest.json=0524b76e141ef1fe...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-crinoid-stereom-gyroid-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 3D Schwarz Diamond TPMS geometry to crystal-plasticity finite-element simulations of twin-band and dislocation arrest under nanoindentation (Yang et al. 2022).",
        "remediation needed: Model intracellular syncytial membrane templating of amorphous calcium carbonate (ACC) precursor vesicles during larval stereom spiculogenesis." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.17e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

